{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20","id":926799,"title":"What else do you want to see from X20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-05T20:10:30-07:00","id":926799,"title":"What else do you want to see from X20?","content":"At this point, the main five games have either come out with are in the works for 20th Anniversary Editions, and now there's murmurs about some of those lines moving on from X20 into White Wolf's 4th Edition. With what we know now, what do you want to see from what's left of X20? There's the smaller gamelines (Hunter, Demon, Kindred of the East, Mummy, maybe even Orpheus) still to go. Would you like more supplements like V20 has been seeing? Do you want historical settings, either old ones done again (DAV20) or those that weren't done before (like the upcoming Victorian Mage, or the long-awaited Dark Ages: Wraith)?<br /> <br /> I'd love to hear everyone's thoughts and wishes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T21:36:27-07:00","id":926834,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see the rest of the originals get their due. Hunter, Demon, Kindred of the East, and Mummy deserve to have their own &quot;anniversary editions&quot; whether that be 20th, or otherwise. My shelf is lonely, and a deluxe Hunter the Reckoning and Demon the Fallen would look fantastic next to some of my other books. The rest of your questions can all be answered with a resounding YES. <br /> <br /> As for will we actually see them? I don't know. I sure hope so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T22:18:34-07:00","id":926857,"title":"","content":"Demon 20th (15th, maybe?) and Dark Ages: Wraith are all I need to be happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T22:35:59-07:00","id":926861,"title":"","content":"I want something to cover Sorcerer, darnit!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T23:13:29-07:00","id":926874,"title":"","content":"Only thing I want after this is Demon 20. And maybe Orpheus 20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T23:17:11-07:00","id":926876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=926874#post926874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only thing I want after this is Demon 20. <b>And maybe Orpheus 20</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The closest you'll probably get for the part in bold is Wr20, which has an appendix on Orpheus and incorporating it into Wraith.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T23:26:07-07:00","id":926883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=926876#post926876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The closest you'll probably get for the part in bold is Wr20, which has an appendix on Orpheus and incorporating it into Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, Orpheus is a popular bugger. I don't think it's likely due to it's inclusion in Wraith, but I'm not closing the door on it either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T23:32:20-07:00","id":926886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=926883#post926883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, Orpheus is a popular bugger. I don't think it's likely due to it's inclusion in Wraith, but I'm not closing the door on it either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we could conceivably see more books on Orpheus-related topics if Wr20 does well. My point is that even with the Wraith curse, you probably won't have to wait until 2023 for more Orpheus stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T01:53:49-07:00","id":926931,"title":"","content":"I'd love to revisit the hilarity of Kindred of the East, but I'd much rather see it using the Exalted 3e as base system rather than WoD 20 - it'd be much better if the game of kung fu vampires worked on a system conductive to high-powered kung fu fights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T01:23:23-07:00","id":927489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=926931#post926931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to revisit the hilarity of Kindred of the East, but I'd much rather see it using the Exalted 3e as base system rather than WoD 20 - it'd be much better if the game of kung fu vampires worked on a system conductive to high-powered kung fu fights.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd prefer a more &quot;action horror&quot; broad conversion option like WOD combat...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T01:37:39-07:00","id":927492,"title":"","content":"If by &quot;action horror&quot; you mean &quot;resolving action scenes is a horror&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T02:39:39-07:00","id":927511,"title":"","content":"I don't really know the Hunter books, but <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Hunter:_The_Reckoning_books\" target=\"_blank\">from the looks of it</a> there is quite a bit of material to work with to make a big book, and possibly a supplement or two. But I don't really know those books, what's in them? I can imagine the the various Hunter Books, same goes for the Storytellers Companion and the Players Guide. Then there are what look like some monster splats (The Moonstruck, The Nocturnal) and what might be a few story books.<br /> <br /> Mummy only has two books IIRC, so that should not be much of a hassle to make one book out of. Demon I already talked about in the D20 topic.<br /> <br /> I don't know anything about Kindred or Orpheus, so no comment there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T03:19:48-07:00","id":927522,"title":"","content":"Kindred of the East is like Big Trouble in Little China with fangs. It's awesome if you like old pulp tales, kung fu movies and/or anime. Not so awesome if you like respectful and factually correct portrayal of Asia, its people and cultures, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T04:33:06-07:00","id":927543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=927522#post927522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred of the East is like Big Trouble in Little China with fangs. It's awesome if you like old pulp tales, kung fu movies and/or anime. Not so awesome if you like respectful and factually correct portrayal of Asia, its people and cultures, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my knowledge on Kindred of the East boils down to &quot;Asian vampires&quot;. I have no idea what kind of books they have, the kind of splats you can play, what kind of opponents you face...<br /> <br /> Would all the stuff in the most recent edition of Kindred fit into one book, or would it be spread out over multiple ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T05:04:28-07:00","id":927558,"title":"","content":"I'm not the most qualified person to answer that question - I gave up on KotE after the corebook because literally nobody I knew showed the least amount of enthusiasm for this game. Damn shame, because the game has much potential, albeit for completely different things than most WoD lines. Which is why I said I'd rather see it using the Exalted system, as of all the oWoD games, KotE is Exalted's most direct protoplast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T06:15:47-07:00","id":927584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=927492#post927492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If by &quot;action horror&quot; you mean &quot;resolving action scenes is a horror&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I mean a book for making combat more reasonable/fun to play out. There's plenty of fiction and desire to play a more action oriented vs murder machine WOD.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=927558#post927558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not the most qualified person to answer that question - I gave up on KotE after the corebook because literally nobody I knew showed the least amount of enthusiasm for this game. Damn shame, because the game has much potential, albeit for completely different things than most WoD lines. Which is why I said I'd rather see it using the Exalted system, as of all the oWoD games, KotE is Exalted's most direct protoplast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really at all. I mean KOTE is pretty solidly &quot;Everything you know about Vampires is a lie&quot; but Masquerade has since Werewolf ended up the weird outlier. Its why people say Demon Vampire and Hunter match up real well and Wraith, Mage, werewolf and changeling match up well. KOTE is the Vampire game that matches up with the cosmology and themes of the Mage, Werewolf, changeling, Wraith World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Its pulpy.. so is mage. Its has solid focus on combat for some splats... hi werewolf. Hell there aren't even special KOTE Only martial arts in it.. unlike Mage and werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said KOTE Could use some serious refinement of the rules for its tranhumanist kungfu zombie themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T07:05:31-07:00","id":927599,"title":"","content":"be the first to agree, KOTE needs some serious refining.<br /> <br /> I dont want the &quot;De mystify asia&quot; Thing a lot of people bring up. Im comfortable with some of us finding the exotic appealing, and refuse to believe theirs anything wrong with that.<br /> <br /> that isnt to say that some revision isnt required, a bit more editing could help.<br /> <br /> And KOTE had a serious problem with having to roll at a difficulty of or against, your own traits, which makes it hard to see how Bohidivastras functioned<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T07:26:46-07:00","id":927606,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify, I'm not saying KotE should be tied into the setting and cosmology of Exalted, at least not more so than it already is (o hai Ebon Dragon!).<br /> <br /> I'm saying it should be remade with Exalted <i>mechanics</i> as a baseline, because Exalted is the Storyteller system game modified for high-power combat and cinematic action, and this kind of system is exactly what KotE needs to realize its full potential.<br /> <br /> Sure, it can be done your way, i.e. by making a separate iteration of Storyteller system that also supports cinematic action and wuxia combat. I just don't see the advantage of this solution compared to using an existing system that achieves the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T15:55:20-07:00","id":927812,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see updated versions of Mummy and Demon, and a book akin to CoD's Dark Era's could be very fun if we don't get specific settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5128-synderryn","name":"Synderryn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T16:46:02-07:00","id":927834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=927606#post927606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify, I'm not saying KotE should be tied into the setting and cosmology of Exalted, at least not more so than it already is (o hai Ebon Dragon!).<br /> <br /> I'm saying it should be remade with Exalted <i>mechanics</i> as a baseline, because Exalted is the Storyteller system game modified for high-power combat and cinematic action, and this kind of system is exactly what KotE needs to realize its full potential.<br /> <br /> Sure, it can be done your way, i.e. by making a separate iteration of Storyteller system that also supports cinematic action and wuxia combat. I just don't see the advantage of this solution compared to using an existing system that achieves the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And what, pray, do you suggest ST's who crossovers do, especialy with conquering San Francisco or driving the Kin-jin out of the Middle Kingdom, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T18:10:28-07:00","id":927878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=927606#post927606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify, I'm not saying KotE should be tied into the setting and cosmology of Exalted, at least not more so than it already is (o hai Ebon Dragon!).<br /> <br /> I'm saying it should be remade with Exalted <i>mechanics</i> as a baseline, because Exalted is the Storyteller system game modified for high-power combat and cinematic action, and this kind of system is exactly what KotE needs to realize its full potential.<br /> <br /> Sure, it can be done your way, i.e. by making a separate iteration of Storyteller system that also supports cinematic action and wuxia combat. I just don't see the advantage of this solution compared to using an existing system that achieves the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get what you are saying but I'm honestly not sure that that is the case. Indiana Gangrel and his League of Extraordinary Vampires is pretty damned pulpy and High action, so could an Alastor or Archon game. And well have you seen werewolf? Or mage when certain Traditions are winning....<br /> <br /> Plus a Broad conversion setup for WOD to Exalted mechanics would finally settle how painfully Caine would get his ass handed to him by a starting Solar PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T18:19:44-07:00","id":927881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=927878#post927878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I get what you are saying but I'm honestly not sure that that is the case. Indiana Gangrel and his League of Extraordinary Vampires is pretty damned pulpy and High action, so could an Alastor or Archon game. And well have you seen werewolf? Or mage when certain Traditions are winning....<br /> <br /> Plus a Broad conversion setup for WOD to Exalted mechanics would finally settle how painfully Caine would get his ass handed to him by a starting Solar PC.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Dont forget the Mark of God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T23:59:33-07:00","id":927986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=927834#post927834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what, pray, do you suggest ST's who crossovers do, especialy with conquering San Francisco or driving the Kin-jin out of the Middle Kingdom, etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the choice between Kuei-Jin being able to star in crossover games, and Kuei-Jin being able to fulfill their potential as over the top anime/wuxia vampires, I'll always go with the latter.<br /> <br /> That said, Masquerade would be even easier to convert to Ex3 than KotE, the powers there are really quite simple mechanically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=927878#post927878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get what you are saying but I'm honestly not sure that that is the case. Indiana Gangrel and his League of Extraordinary Vampires is pretty damned pulpy and High action, so could an Alastor or Archon game. And well have you seen werewolf? Or mage when certain Traditions are winning....</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure we're not so much disagreeing as we're talking past each other. I never said other games couldn't get converted in a similar way, just that KotE is the one game which I really think needs to make this transition.<br /> <br /> If OPP ever releases &quot;WoD action mode&quot; set of alternate rules, I'll definitely be interested regardless of how much or how little it takes from Exalted. It's just that I really like Ex3 as a base system for this kind of play, and am already quite familiar with it, so it'd benefit me more to have an Ex3 conversion than it would to get a completely new action-oriented system for oWoD.<br /> <br /> I hope I'm making sense here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus a Broad conversion setup for WOD to Exalted mechanics would finally settle how painfully Caine would get his ass handed to him by a starting Solar PC. </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://cdn.meme.am/instances/500x/55335332.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T00:48:27-07:00","id":928006,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see Kindred of the East as its own game of insane undead wuxia action rather than a racist footnote in oWoD that stepped pretty heavily on Vampire's toes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T01:11:15-07:00","id":928010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=927878#post927878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus a Broad conversion setup for WOD to Exalted mechanics would finally settle how painfully Caine would get his ass handed to him by a starting Solar PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you stat Caine beyond writing the words &quot;You lose&quot; on a character sheet you've already messed up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T01:48:51-07:00","id":928018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=927986#post927986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the choice between Kuei-Jin being able to star in crossover games, and Kuei-Jin being able to fulfill their potential as over the top anime/wuxia vampires, I'll always go with the latter.<br /> <br /> That said, Masquerade would be even easier to convert to Ex3 than KotE, the powers there are really quite simple mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I personally think of KOTE as more the BEAST of CWOD and thus has a strong requirement for Crossovers. That any version of it that isn't fairly crossover compatable is missing a major chunk of it.. and a big way in which its NOT Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty sure we're not so much disagreeing as we're talking past each other. I never said other games couldn't get converted in a similar way, just that KotE is the one game which I really think needs to make this transition.<br /> <br /> If OPP ever releases &quot;WoD action mode&quot; set of alternate rules, I'll definitely be interested regardless of how much or how little it takes from Exalted. It's just that I really like Ex3 as a base system for this kind of play, and am already quite familiar with it, so it'd benefit me more to have an Ex3 conversion than it would to get a completely new action-oriented system for oWoD.<br /> <br /> I hope I'm making sense here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> </div> </div> </div>I think KOTE is as I said very dependent upon crossover to get the most out of it. Its not just a game of Wuxia Transhuman Zombies but its also the game of grand supernatural politicing. It can be a game of grand supernatural martial arts action.. or it can be a game about playing a dangerous game of politics where everyone hates eachother but puts up a polite face. Where you can entreat with the Kitsune and Nezumi rather than &quot;RAAAAWR WYRRRRRRM&quot; of the Garou nation, where you act as intermediary between the Living and the Dead, where you deal with Lightning People and Little Gods in the face of the Yama Kings corruption and mankinds growing indifference.<br /> <br /> So as a long term KOTE player a game that was even less crossover friendly than the current version would be practically useless.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the otherhand a &quot;WoD Combat 20&quot; that gives a conversion for Wod20 to Exalted 3e rules(Scion/Conntinuum storytelling) would both help with Wuxia KOTE games.. and WUxia Akashic games and Pulpy Etherite games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=928010#post928010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you stat Caine beyond writing the words &quot;You lose&quot; on a character sheet you've already messed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted's premise is your character is personally responsible for Beating a bunch of things that had as their stats &quot;you lose&quot; On their sheets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T02:36:49-07:00","id":928024,"title":"","content":"I don't think we'll reach consensus here, as I have very little interest in oWoD these days, and I'd much rather see KotE as a self-contained exotic urban fantasy setting than a part of oWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T02:42:59-07:00","id":928026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=928024#post928024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we'll reach consensus here, as I have very little interest in oWoD these days, and I'd much rather see KotE as a self-contained exotic urban fantasy setting than a part of oWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could put it in a different setting, but it still requires a kitchen sink. Its very much a game that is significantly lessened by not having other monsters. Its very much the CWOD's Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T07:34:00-07:00","id":928107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=928024#post928024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we'll reach consensus here, as I have very little interest in oWoD these days, and I'd much rather see KotE as a self-contained exotic urban fantasy setting than a part of oWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always considered Mage to occupy the &quot;better left jettisoned&quot; game in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T07:46:21-07:00","id":928120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=928107#post928107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always considered Mage to occupy the &quot;better left jettisoned&quot; game in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say Mage is as bad as KOTE For needing others, it can fill in the gaps with itown cosmology(Bygones, spirits, sorcerers) but it too needs a fairly crowded universe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T07:52:19-07:00","id":928126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=928120#post928120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't say Mage is as bad as KOTE For needing others, it can fill in the gaps with itown cosmology(Bygones, spirits, sorcerers) but it too needs a fairly crowded universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring more to the record scratching difference of setting involved with having to accommodate Mage's &quot;all things are magic, technology is just a consensus rote&quot; standpoint on how existence works. Then there;s the matter of it trying to be Ars Magica Modern, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:56:56-07:00","id":928270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=927543#post927543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, my knowledge on Kindred of the East boils down to &quot;Asian vampires&quot;. I have no idea what kind of books they have, the kind of splats you can play, what kind of opponents you face...</div> </div> </div> </div>KotE has one of the largest WoD lines outside of the Big Five and Dark Ages. In terms of books its got all the WoD standards, the Core Book, the Companion, the individual Splat books, a City Book, the Minion Book, a Dark Ages and Victorian add-on, etc. About the only thing it does lack is a dedicated Enemy Book. The best they have is the <i>Thousand Hells</i> book but that's more on the titular realms and their masters than their servants that the Kuei-Jin fight against.<br /> <br /> As for what kind of splats you play as, well the Kuei-Jin do not have Clans or Bloodlines or any variation of the Blood as Cainites do. There is one rare exception to this but other than they are all the same species. The variation in them comes in the form of the various Dharmas they practice. The Dharmas are like Paths of Enlightenment but they are actual paths that lead to Enlightenment. In fact unlike Cainities that have built in limitations if they do not commit Diablerie, Kuei-Jin have no such limit and can become very powerful. In fact in the Week of Nightmares the three eldest Kuei-Jin on Earth battled [Ravnos] for days.<br /> <br /> The Kuei-Jin are a different breed from Cainites. The short version is that they people who died and who's soul lingered. However instead of ending up in the Underworld as a wraith would, they were dragged down into one of the 1000 Hells to be tortured for all eternity. But their soul was able to escape, clawing its way back into their remains, rising from their grave as Kuei-Jin. Most start out as savage monsters that have to be captured and have sense beaten back into them and shown the basics of a Dharma which in turn is what they use to hold back their version of the Beast. Unlike Cainites blood does not actually sustain them in and of itself but rather the Chi within blood does. And as they progress up their Dharma they gain the ability to gain it from other sources rather than blood.<br /> <br /> Of the Dharmas, there are the Main Five and a number of lesser 'Heretical' Dharmas, called that because the Courts of China, the most powerful of the Kuei-Jin support only the Main Five and legends around their origins. And they are the splats of KotE instead of Clans and Bloodlines. Like I said, the Dharmas are philosophical paths with wildly different outlooks and embody different aspects of the Kuei-Jin being. For example the Devil-Tigers embody the P'o, the dark part of the soul we recognize as the Shadow or even the Beast. They are generally wicked sadists that revel in inflicting pain and suffering on others though only on the wicked as they style themselves as devils that tempt and punish the sinful. Another Dharma, the Trashing Dragons, embody Yang, the Chi of Life. As a result they are among the most passionate and human-like of the Kuei-Jin, throwing themselves into the joys and thrills of life.<br /> <br /> As for enemies, there are the servants of the Yama Kings, the rulers of the 1000 Hells and their various minions, including the Akuma, Kuei-Jin that willingly serve them, the Beast Courts of Asia, a collection of local Garou and other Changing Breeds though they don't have the utter hatred for the KJ as the Western Garou do for Cainites, various Hunter groups, namely the Shih and Strike Force Zero, Cainites and just about anything else that is present in their domains.<br /> <br /> And of course each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would all the stuff in the most recent edition of Kindred fit into one book, or would it be spread out over multiple ones? </div> </div> </div>There's only one Edition of KotE. Could all the important stuff be put in one book? Yes, as much as any of the recent x20 Rule Books have done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:42:56-07:00","id":928306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=928126#post928126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was referring more to the record scratching difference of setting involved with having to accommodate Mage's &quot;all things are magic, technology is just a consensus rote&quot; standpoint on how existence works. Then there;s the matter of it trying to be Ars Magica Modern, too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd disagree that Mage presents a pure Consentual reality vs.. a reality effected by human belief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T15:12:55-07:00","id":929407,"title":"","content":"An index would be nice. V20 and W20 both had them, but M20 as well as some recent books (H:TV's Mortal Remains as well as Beast) did not have them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T16:56:29-07:00","id":929455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=929407#post929407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An index would be nice. V20 and W20 both had them, but M20 as well as some recent books (H:TV's Mortal Remains as well as Beast) did not have them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you download the 'final' versions of them? Because they don't put indexes in the advance release versions, they add it after they get the errata taken care of (in case pages change). Just go back to Drivethru and download the latest version of the pdf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 07-10-2016, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T00:48:03-07:00","id":929608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=929455#post929455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you download the 'final' versions of them? Because they don't put indexes in the advance release versions, they add it after they get the errata taken care of (in case pages change). Just go back to Drivethru and download the latest version of the pdf.</div> </div> </div> </div>... whoops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T21:07:20-07:00","id":944109,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see something specifically supporting crossovers.<br /> <br /> A crossover-heavy city book or adventure book.<br /> <br /> A general guide for running crossover games, with conversion rules and several different &quot;spins&quot; of canon that account for contradictions in different ways. Say, three to six unifying theories for reconciling how things like the Triat, consensus reality, and the War in Heaven relate to the WoD as a whole, each with a collection of places, characters, splats, and/or story hooks that play on the connections.<br /> <br /> A &quot;zoomed out&quot; version of the WoD that keeps the basic political layout and as much of the history as possible, but compresses it into a single book with simplified rules, maybe Exalted-like, maybe d20 or FATE, and each of the game lines as a single splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5553-mr-sluagh","name":"Mr. Sluagh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T21:23:08-07:00","id":944115,"title":"","content":"I do not want to see Exalted 3e 'you go first, you win' combat system. I would rather see them scrap the entire combat system and 'adapt' the combat system, and martial arts rules, from Shadowrun 4th edition. Martial Arts would probably be a Background, with each level giving you a combat bonus, and you could just purchase martial arts techniques for 1 freebie point or 2 experience points each, with no more than your level on the Martial Arts Background. Your maximum combat bonus would be equal to your relevant ability. I would also not mind some sensible version of WoD Combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T17:02:16-07:00","id":944596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/926799-what-else-do-you-want-to-see-from-x20?p=944115#post944115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not want to see Exalted 3e 'you go first, you win' combat system.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really an accurate description of it at all. A hugely favorably Join Battle roll requires a rather extensive pile of dice; just cap the elder Vampire and whatever's Abilities at 5 and go easy on Attributes, and things should stay within a more manageable zone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would rather see them scrap the entire combat system and 'adapt' the combat system, and martial arts rules, from Shadowrun 4th edition. Martial Arts would probably be a Background, with each level giving you a combat bonus, and you could just purchase martial arts techniques for 1 freebie point or 2 experience points each, with no more than your level on the Martial Arts Background. Your maximum combat bonus would be equal to your relevant ability. I would also not mind some sensible version of WoD Combat. </div> </div> </div>SR4 is like CoD with even more cumbersome rules and out of control dice pools, located in even less sensible places in the book..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}